# NOTICE

superred-claim-injecagent

This module is a port of InjecAgent into the superred red-teaming framework.
Original code in this module (the superred adaptation: the pure judge, task
model, factories, loaders, and tests) is licensed MIT (see LICENSE). It bundles
benchmark data and reproduces evaluation logic from InjecAgent; the upstream MIT
license text is preserved verbatim in
`src/injecagent_claim/data/INJECAGENT_LICENSE` (and `LICENSES/InjecAgent-MIT.txt`).

## Upstream: InjecAgent

- Project: InjecAgent — "Benchmarking Indirect Prompt Injections in
  Tool-Integrated Large Language Model Agents"
- Repository: https://github.com/uiuc-kang-lab/InjecAgent (commit f19c9f2)
- Paper: Zhan, Liang, Ying, Kang, ACL Findings 2024 (arXiv:2403.02691).
- License: MIT
- Copyright (c) 2023 Qiusi Zhan

### Bundled data (vendored verbatim, MIT)

Under `src/injecagent_claim/data/`:

- `test_cases_dh_base.json`, `test_cases_dh_enhanced.json`,
  `test_cases_ds_base.json`, `test_cases_ds_enhanced.json` — all 1,054 base test
  cases (dh 510, ds 544) plus the enhanced-setting variants, byte-for-byte as
  upstream ships them.
- `INJECAGENT_LICENSE` — verbatim upstream MIT license.

The tool *schemas* the agent sees are NOT bundled here — they live in the paired
`superred-target-injecagent` package (and carry a separate ToolEmu Apache-2.0
attribution). This claim vendors only InjecAgent's own synthetic test cases.

### Ported evaluation logic (MIT)

The deterministic prompted (text ReAct) and finetuned (function-calling)
attack-success evaluators and the attack-success-rate scoring are ported from
upstream `src/output_parsing.py` and `src/utils.py` into
`src/injecagent_claim/judge.py` as pure, LLM-free functions over the agent's
output. Deviations are documented in `ASSUMPTIONS.md`.

